// A duplicate top-level fn used to be accepted: the VM kept the LAST
// definition while the C backend emitted the FIRST (its fn_map is
// first-wins), so the same file printed `2` on the VM and `1 on the C
// backend (audit §3.10).
// EXPECT-ERROR: duplicate function 'main'
fn main() { print(1) }
fn main() { print(2) }
